## Principal provisioning permission

The permission catalog must also contain:

```text
principals.manage
```

This permission is intended for Super Admin Principal management.

Super Admin currently receives all defined permissions through:

```text
Object.values(PERMISSIONS)
```

Therefore adding a new permission automatically makes it available to Super Admin without changing the Super Admin role mapping.

Principal, Teacher, and Student must NOT automatically receive `principals.manage`.

Architecture:

```text
permissions.ts
↓
Permission definitions

rolePermissions.ts
↓
Role → Permission mapping

permission.middleware.ts
↓
requirePermission()

JWT
↓
Authentication
↓
User Role
↓
Role Permissions
↓
Required Permission
↓
Allow / Deny
```

