# 13.1 PRINCIPAL PROVISIONING / SECURITY

Principal creation must NOT be public.

Target API:

```text
POST /api/admin/principals
```

Security chain:

```text
authenticateToken
↓
requireRole('super_admin')
↓
requirePermission(PRINCIPALS_MANAGE)
↓
Principal Controller
↓
Principal Service
↓
User Model
```

Input may contain:

```json
{
  "fullName": "Principal Name",
  "email": "principal@school.com",
  "phone": "03XXXXXXXXX",
  "password": "password",
  "branchId": "BRANCH_OBJECT_ID"
}
```

The client MUST NOT be allowed to choose:

```text
role
```

Backend automatically sets:

```text
role: principal
```

Backend must enforce:

* authenticated caller
* Super Admin role
* `principals.manage` permission
* required fields
* valid email
* valid password
* valid MongoDB ObjectId
* branch exists
* branch is active
* email uniqueness
* password hashing
* valid branch assignment
* no duplicate Principal account where business rules prohibit it
* password never returned in API response

Success must only be returned after database confirmation.

