# 36. DEVELOPMENT COMMUNICATION RULE

When working on this project:

* Give clear step-by-step instructions.
* Do not give unnecessary information.
* Do not jump multiple development steps at once.
* Give one small actionable task at a time during implementation.
* Wait for command/output/result before proceeding.
* Never assume a command succeeded without confirmation.
* If an error occurs, fix the current step first.
* Do not move to the next feature until the current feature is fully complete.
* Preserve existing working code.
* Do not modify `main`.
* Do not expose secrets.
* Do not ask the user to share `.env`.
* Do not redo completed Step 12 work unnecessarily.
* Keep current working implementation as the source of truth.
* Never silently remove existing functionality while implementing a new feature.

